  "derivation": "w = 0xabc | 1<<16 | 1<<18 | 1<<19 | 1<<20 = 0x1d0abc. Table 22/23: in `u = d.eol << 20` the 32-bit target size propagates to the shift and then to its left-hand side, so u = 0x100000, not 0 (a tool that shifts at 1 bit gets 0). Likewise v. Unpacking: (w >> 16) = 0x1d, 4 bits 0xd; (w >> 17) = 0xe, bit 0; (w >> 18) = 7, bit 1."
